WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Breaking news, everyone. If you ever had

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.640
something wrong with your credit report,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.560
like a collection you already paid, or

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.360
an item on your credit report that

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.600
wasn't yours, you need to watch this

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:17.040
because the CFPB just changed the rules

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.960
on how you can fight back. And here's

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.240
the question I want you to sit with over

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.000
these few minutes. What happens to your

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.480
credit score when the agency that's

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.080
supposed to protect you suddenly makes

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.240
it harder for you to protect yourself?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.960
Now, most people believe that the CFPB

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.400
is on their side. That's the whole

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.840
reason why they actually exist. If the

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.920
credit bureau ignored your dispute, you

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.720
would file a complaint with the CFPB and

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.400
they would put pressure on the credit

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:47.800
bureau to investigate. Well, that's all

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:49.920
over. As of June of 2026, the CFPB

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.600
rolled out what they called a major

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.920
overhaul to their system. And when you

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.880
actually read what it does, it's not an

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.320
improvement, it's a barrier. Now, here's

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.920
what changed. Now, you have to go back

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.680
and dispute with the credit reporting

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.640
agency directly. Now, this is the same

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.120
company that put the negative

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:13.480
information on your credit report in the

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:15.920
first place before the CFPB will even

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.840
accept your complaint. Now, the National

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.760
Consumer Law Center is already calling

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.840
it out. This is making it harder for

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.400
consumers to make reports against the

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.720
credit reporting agencies. Now, think

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.960
about that for a second. The bureau that

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.720
was established to protect you just

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.360
handed power back to the people you were

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.440
complaining about. Now, I'm going to

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.280
walk through what this exactly means for

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.240
your credit scores and the three things

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.320
you need to do right now to protect

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.640
yourself. And the last one is the worst

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.040
one because it's the one that most

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.400
people are going to get caught up by it.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:54.840
What the CFPB just did is added a whole

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:57.560
'nother layer between you and any

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.600
resolution. You dispute with the bureau,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:03.760
you wait for them to accept the dispute,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.040
and then process the dispute, and then,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.560
only if they don't fix the error, can

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.320
you escalate your complaint. Every

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.920
single step of this new process is

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.920
time-consuming,

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.840
and time is the only thing that your

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.800
credit score cannot get back. And here's

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.000
what actually happens when a negative

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:25.600
item sit on your credit report. Every

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.640
collection, you lose 50 to 100 points.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.280
And a late payment can knock your credit

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:33.880
score down from 60 to 110 points. While

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.480
you wait, stuck in this new dispute

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.880
loop, that damage is just sitting there,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.560
costing you every single time someone

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.000
pulls your credit. A car loan, a

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:47.560
mortgage, a credit card, costing you

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.520
higher interest, and even a denial of

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.880
credit altogether. This is all leading

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.200
you with worse terms with the banks. And

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.040
this is a setup against consumers

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.520
because they made it harder for you to

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:01.320
challenge this information, and who

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.519
benefits? It's not you, it's actually

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.280
the banks that benefits from higher

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:08.200
interest rates, and you getting worse

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.239
lending terms. Now, I'm not going to

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.200
leave you hanging because as a consumer,

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.120
you still have rights, and I'm going to

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.800
give you three things you need to do

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:18.600
right now to protect yourself. And if

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.000
you like staying up-to-date with credit

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.400
information to protect your credit

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.959
scores and banking changes, feel free to

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.040
subscribe to the channel. Now, let's

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:28.320
jump to step number one to protect

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:31.400
yourself. Step number one, always

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:34.040
dispute in writing, never dispute with

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.680
the credit bureaus online. You must

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:39.239
dispute in writing directly to the

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:42.280
credit bureaus, sending it certified

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:44.600
mail. You want to keep proof to protect

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.400
yourself. Keep that record. When you

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:50.080
dispute online, they actually have the

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.480
record of your dispute, and you lose all

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.240
power and all of your rights. Now, with

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.560
this new setup with the CFPD and this

00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:00.680
dispute process before you can file a

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:04.000
complaint, you must be able to prove it.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:07.640
So, only do your disputes in writing and

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.560
by U.S. certified mail. Step number two,

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:13.240
you want to file your dispute with the

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:16.040
credit bureaus and with the furnisher of

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:18.320
the information. So, for instance, if

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:21.200
you have a collection on your credit

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:24.000
report, that collection company is the

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:26.040
furnisher of that information. And now,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.560
you want to save time. So, with that

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.560
collection company, you want to send

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.080
them a debt validation letter. That is

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.640
your right under the law to make them

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.160
prove they have a legal right to collect

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:42.480
on that debt because most of them buy

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:45.080
that debt as a third party. And once you

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:48.200
send them that debt validation letter,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.800
they must provide you proof within 30

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:53.680
days they have a legal right to collect

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:56.680
on that debt. Make sure that when you

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.600
send those letters, never sign your

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:01.440
signature because then they can take

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:05.400
your signature and put it on a contract.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:08.440
Make sure you always send it to them by

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:11.360
certified mail. You must prove it. If

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.960
they don't respond to you in 30 days,

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.000
then you have a right to have that taken

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.120
off of your credit report. So, you want

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.560
to do both processes at one time. If you

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.480
need a debt validation letter, I do have

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:25.160
them at my website. I'll leave that link

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:28.280
in the description below. Step number

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:31.080
three, you want to find the errors in

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:33.160
that negative information or item on

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.280
your credit report reporting against

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.240
you. So, look at all three of your

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.400
credit reports and find the

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:42.000
inconsistencies. Remember, under the

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:44.440
Fair Credit Reporting Act, for them to

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:48.760
report that against you, it has to be

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:52.160
100% complete and accurate. Even if it's

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:54.840
true, if it's not reporting completely

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.960
and accurately, they cannot report the

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.800
information. So, you need to do factual

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:04.080
disputes. Find the errors, [music] and

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:07.000
then you want to do at least two

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:10.280
disputes with the credit bureaus and

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:13.600
have your proof. Send it certified mail.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:16.880
Send your proof to that you have sent

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.600
that creditor or that furnisher that

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.640
letter too. So, keep those

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:24.680
documentations, and if that information

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:28.360
is not updated or removed, now you can

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:31.560
go to the CFPB, and you want to present

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:34.080
your evidence. So, if you have sent this

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:37.919
certified mail, you want to go to the

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:40.040
post office website, and then put in

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:42.560
your certified tracking numbers, and

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:45.120
find the date that they received it, and

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.640
print it out. That is your proof that

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.840
you sent it to them, and they actually

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:53.320
received that letter, and that's when

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:55.840
the clock start ticking. So, make sure

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:58.880
you always demand that these credit

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:02.320
bureaus write you back. Like, with

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:04.440
Experian, they have an online, and they

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:07.680
will sometimes try to get you to click

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:10.560
on those disputes online to only try to

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:13.200
do it in the system with your

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.080
investigation results. Do not accept

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.720
that. They're trying to steal your

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:20.040
rights. Demand that they send it back to

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.720
you in writing. If they don't, and they

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.200
put it in that system, that's on them.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:28.000
That 30-day clock have already started,

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.000
and they must actually delete that

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.840
information. Now, I've been doing this

